// Headless execution in the interpreter, which generates no code.
//
// The interpreter emits nothing, so this package holds only what it has to be
// *told* rather than shown: a primitive whose meaning is a schedule, which no
// visual tree can express and no host widget stands in for.
//
// It is a package in lib/ with no Go behind it. What runs a program built for
// it is the compiler's own interpreter, which `sngl run` and `sngl test` reach
// for every pair `--lang none` leaves untranslated.
